From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yi Xie <imxieyi@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 09:21:42 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] zink: give a fence wait one deadline

fence_wait() waits for the submission of a batch with the timeout it is
given, and then waits for the GPU with the whole timeout again: a wait
of 100 ms could take nearly 200 ms when the submission used most of the
first. The wait for the GPU now gets what is left.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/gallium/drivers/zink/zink_fence.c | 7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/gallium/drivers/zink/zink_fence.c b/src/gallium/drivers/zink/zink_fence.c
index 6aac14608888f91cd87e32dbc147a8ae7b32e71e..1bf974f15080ed50fea4af01d0ff2a10729c945e 100644
--- a/src/gallium/drivers/zink/zink_fence.c
+++ b/src/gallium/drivers/zink/zink_fence.c
@@ -139,6 +139,13 @@ fence_wait(struct zink_screen *screen, struct zink_fence *fence, uint64_t timeou
       int64_t abs_timeout = os_time_get_absolute_timeout(timeout_ns);
       if (!util_queue_fence_wait_timeout(&bs->flush_completed, abs_timeout))
          return false;
+      /* the wait for the GPU gets what is left of the time, not all of it
+       * again after the submission took part of it
+       */
+      if (timeout_ns && abs_timeout != OS_TIMEOUT_INFINITE) {
+         int64_t time_ns = os_time_get_nano();
+         timeout_ns = abs_timeout > time_ns ? abs_timeout - time_ns : 0;
+      }
    }
 
    assert(fence->batch_id);
